---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "associativity — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>associativity</h1>
    <p>associativity is how freely ideas trigger other ideas in your mind. a sight, a word, a snippet of conversation can chain into a cascade of thoughts. adhd brains are high in associativity (constant chain-reaction thinking); this can feel chaotic, but it's also the source of creative leaps. neurotypical brains often have lower associativity and benefit from deliberately cultivating it.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>free association: say the first word that comes to mind, then the next, and so on</li>
      <li>random stimuli: pick random words or images and force connections to your problem</li>
      <li>forced connections: link unrelated ideas and justify the link (e.g., "how is adhd like jazz?")</li>
      <li>mind mapping: start with a central idea and branch freely, no filtering</li>
      <li>recognize when associativity is creative flow vs. when it's distraction; context matters</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="care">high associativity without focus is tangent-chasing; low associativity without elasticity is rigid thinking. you need both.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
